# Constructor arguments the .pyi marks omittable that the binding requires, and
# that doppler cannot fix on its own. Both faces are jm-generated, so there is
# no local change that makes them agree — only the upstream one. Each entry is
# `Class.param`, and check_init_param_optionality.py reports an entry that has
# stopped diverging, so this list cannot quietly outlive its reason.
#
# just-makeit#845. NOT the same reason these were first listed, and the
# original exit condition was wrong, so it is written out here.
#
# They went on the list for #823 Ask C / #805 SS-H: a capsule init-param
# rejected Py_None unconditionally, so `Capture(clock=None)` raised while the
# stub rendered `= ...`. The note said "remove both when the pin carries Ask C;
# the TypeError simply becomes a working call."
#
# 0.53.0 carries it and `clock=None` now works -- verified, and the C has
# always taken NULL to mean "no time base stated". But **omitting** the
# argument still raises `missing required argument 'clock'`, and the stub still
# says `= ...`. Accepting None and being omittable are different axes (jm's own
# 0.53.0 notes say so); only the first was fixed. So the divergence these
# entries describe is unchanged and they stay.
#
# Remove them when the STUB stops advertising a default the binding does not
# honour -- just-makeit#845, which also reports a worse sibling: when a capsule
# param is declared before a defaulted one, the stub and kwlist disagree on
# ORDER too. doppler is not exposed to that half; ours is declared last.
MemoryCapture.clock
Capture.clock
